{"id": "EUVD-2026-83211", "enisaUuid": "87739141-2a8a-3e5e-bc2f-b4ae82e53934", "description": "Icinga 2 is an open source monitoring system. From 2.4 until 2.14.9, 2.15.4, and 2.16.2, the /v1/objects API writes attacker-controlled template names into generated configuration without escaping them. An authenticated ApiUser with an objects/create/* permission can inject Icinga 2 DSL configuration, escape the intended object, create additional objects, and exceed the user's assigned privileges. This issue is fixed in versions 2.14.9, 2.15.4, and 2.16.2.", "datePublished": "2026-09-18T17:24:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-18T18:05:44", "baseScore": 7.2, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://github.com/Icinga/icinga2/security/advisories/GHSA-jgqj-x5j9-vgcm", "https://github.com/Icinga/icinga2/pull/10910", "https://github.com/Icinga/icinga2/commit/125b7734e84d03f09b79d36c270152b11629a8c5", "https://github.com/Icinga/icinga2/commit/af4b36e6464b9b214bed270a53d6474cf91eb441", "https://github.com/Icinga/icinga2/commit/eec0d90e8303376fe772b3e4a04e3b064a44cf30", "https://github.com/Icinga/icinga2/commit/faf0450962ad678397991cfdf041810feafa71e7", "https://github.com/Icinga/icinga2/releases/tag/v2.14.9", "https://github.com/Icinga/icinga2/releases/tag/v2.15.4", "https://github.com/Icinga/icinga2/releases/tag/v2.16.2", "https://icinga.com/blog/icinga2-security-release-v2-16-2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-61552"], "assigner": "GitHub_M", "epss": 0.9, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "79802d81-6f77-3e87-ac95-8563da51d5ea", "product": {"name": "icinga2", "vendor": {"name": "Icinga"}}, "product_version": "2.16.0, < 2.16.2"}, {"id": "a1537e7d-4e6e-3310-a83b-bd475ca4060b", "product": {"name": "icinga2", "vendor": {"name": "Icinga"}}, "product_version": "2.15.0, < 2.15.4"}, {"id": "d8562ecc-8e7c-3e3e-a3f9-624f30b643ba", "product": {"name": "icinga2", "vendor": {"name": "Icinga"}}, "product_version": "2.4, < 2.14.9"}], "enis